@startuml
autonumber
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #2F5D7C
  LifeLineBorderColor #2F5D7C
  LifeLineBackgroundColor #F8FBFF
  ParticipantBorderColor #2F5D7C
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #EAF4FF
}

actor "Framework E2E\nprovisioner" as Test
participant "Containerlab E2E\nlifecycle" as Lab
participant "Framework network /\nendpoint managers" as Framework
participant "OVSDB management API" as Mgmt
database "OVN NBDB" as NB
participant "ovn-northd" as Northd
database "OVN SBDB" as SB
participant "GoBGP Netlink\nnode-agent" as Agent
participant "managed gobgpd\n(k8gobgp DaemonSet)" as GoBGP
participant "External FRR peer\n+ remote workload" as FRR
participant "Owned Linux\nNetlink state" as Netlink
participant "ovn-controller" as Controller
participant "OVN/OVS dataplane" as OVS

note over Test,Agent
  This is a one-chassis Framework test. It does not invoke
  evpn-cni, Multus, CNI ADD/CHECK/DEL, or a NAD.
end note

== Disposable laboratory ==
Test -> Lab : reserve exact topology; deploy native kind + FRR
Lab -> Lab : verify ownership, readiness and management CA
Lab --> Test : private kubeconfig and environment receipts
Test -> Test : deploy OVN/OVS and managed k8gobgp
note over Test,GoBGP
  BGPConfiguration CRD -> k8gobgp reconciliation -> managed gobgpd.
  Manager + daemon share one upstream DaemonSet image.
  Framework clients use local Unix gRPC; upstream Netlink writers are disabled.
end note

== Framework provisioning ==
Test -> Mgmt : AddNetwork(logical switch)
Mgmt -> NB : create Framework-owned logical switch
NB --> Mgmt : network status
Mgmt --> Test : success
Test -> Framework : Ensure endpoint A/B
Framework -> Framework : create identity-owned netns and veth attachments
Framework -> NB : ensure owned Logical_Switch_Ports
NB --> Framework : LSP state
Framework -> OVS : ensure identity-owned local OVS attachment
Framework --> Test : endpoint identities and interface receipts
NB -> Northd : logical network / port configuration
Northd -> SB : asynchronous logical flows and Port_Binding
SB --> Controller : chassis-bound Port_Binding
Controller -> OVS : claim local binding; program forwarding

== GoBGP EVPN exchange ==
Agent -> Netlink : read native local advertisement FDB / neighbors
Netlink --> Agent : complete dump plus validated OVN endpoint provenance
Agent -> GoBGP : AddPath local Type-2 MAC and MAC/IP; retain UUID
GoBGP -> FRR : BGP EVPN Type-2 updates
FRR -> GoBGP : remote Type-2 route
Agent -> GoBGP : ListPath complete EVPN RIB
GoBGP --> Agent : authoritative remote route snapshot
Agent -> Agent : validate route identity, RT, VNI, and next hop
Agent -> Netlink : apply receipt-owned FDB/neighbor state
Netlink --> Agent : ownership receipts
Controller -> Netlink : observe Linux EVPN integration state
Controller -> OVS : program OVN tunnel/flow/BUM state

== Workload forwarding and evidence ==
Test -> OVS : ping from local endpoint to remote workload
OVS -> FRR : forward through OVN/OVS and EVPN overlay
FRR --> OVS : return traffic through OVN/OVS
OVS --> Test : bidirectional traffic result
Test -> Test : correlate five packet captures and runtime snapshots

== Withdrawal and survivor verification ==
Test -> Framework : delete local endpoint A
Framework -> NB : remove endpoint A LSP
Agent -> Agent : asynchronously observe authoritative local removal
Agent -> GoBGP : DeletePath exact owned UUIDs for A
GoBGP -> FRR : withdraw endpoint A
Test -> FRR : verify A withdrawn and B retained
Test -> OVS : ping surviving endpoint B and remote workload
OVS -> FRR : verify survivor forwarding in both directions
Test -> Framework : delete remaining endpoint B
Agent -> Agent : observe endpoint B removal and reconcile export
Agent -> GoBGP : DeletePath exact owned UUIDs for B
Test -> Test : wait for exporter ownership receipts to empty
Test -> Mgmt : DelNetwork(logical switch)
Mgmt -> NB : remove Framework-owned logical switch
Test -> Netlink : verify owned state removed; preserve foreign state
Test -> Lab : collect diagnostics; destroy exact owned topology
Lab --> Test : owned resources absent; unrelated resources preserved

note over SB,OVS
  NB-to-SB binding and ovn-controller programming are asynchronous.
  The test checks resulting binding, OVS state, real traffic, and
  packet captures; an API success alone is not a forwarding PASS.
end note

note over Agent,Netlink
  Type-2 import/export is explicitly configured for this test and
  remains disabled by default in the standard deployment.
end note
@enduml
